{
  "comment": "The swim lanes /swimlanes ranks (swimlanes.py). A lane is anything someone can hold in their head that takes more than a couple of prompts and one pull request to finish - a vessel, a game, a section of the app shell, a mechanical system - never a task. Vessels come from the roster (every Assets/Resources/ElementalAbilityMaps/<Vessel>.asset) and games from the shipped cards (every Assets/_SO_Assets/Games/ArcadeGame<Name>.asset): they need no entry here; give one an alias when its files use another name, or list it as retired. A shell section or a system is a key, a name, the tokens a file name or folder carries (matched at a word or CamelCase boundary, so 'Ratel' never matches 'generateLattice') and path prefixes; add one in the same commit that starts multi-PR work nobody's lane covers. One that is truly closed out gets `archived` (\"<date>, <who>: why\") and leaves the board; delete it only once nobody needs its history. 'verdicts' is where a PERSON says a lane is polished or rough; a verdict beats the measured polish signals and is written with `swimlanes.py set`. Any collaborator may add a lane or a token; a lane that grows too wide (most commits touch it) stops telling people apart, so keep tokens specific and add a system only when work on it collides in practice.",
